<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-23408] Calcite. &apos;Typeof&apos; should fail in case of incorrect parameter.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-23408</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Reproducer:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
&lt;span class=&quot;code-comment&quot;&gt;//Should &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;throw&lt;/span&gt; an exception.
&lt;/span&gt;assertQuery(&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;SELECT TYPEOF(CAST(&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&apos;NOT_A_NUMBER&apos;&lt;/span&gt; AS INTEGER))&quot;&lt;/span&gt;).returns(&lt;span class=&quot;code-quote&quot;&gt;&quot;INTEGER&quot;&lt;/span&gt;).check();
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Adoption of #&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-18761&quot; title=&quot;Sql. TypeOf can short-circuit only when its argument is a constant expression.&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-18761&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-18761&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
